 r←MinimumVersionOfDyalog;cfg
⍝ Returns the minimum version of Dyalog APL this package requires.\\
⍝ It comes from the package config, so there is just one source of truth: `Make` injects that
⍝ very same value into the user command script; see `InjectListOfObjectsIntoUserCommandScript`.
 r←''
 :If 0<##.⎕NC'TatinVars.CONFIG'
     cfg←##.TatinVars.CONFIG
 :ElseIf 0<##.##.⎕NC'TatinVars.CONFIG'
     cfg←##.##.TatinVars.CONFIG
 :Else
     :Return                        ⍝ Not loaded by Tatin: no config, so no restriction either
 :EndIf
 r←(⎕JSON⍠('Dialect' 'JSON5')⊢cfg).minimumAplVersion
⍝Done
